					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12606396#post-4381351</guid>
				<title>Junior Staff - Site Criticism</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12606396/scp-6009-j#post-4381351</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 29 Sep 2019 20:12:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Tanhony</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>776854</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p><strong>NOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO</strong></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Tanhony&nbsp;rambles</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">TURN&nbsp;IT&nbsp;OFF</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>NOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO</strong></p> <blockquote> <p>Object Class: Neutralized</p> </blockquote> <p>Oh, thank god.</p> <blockquote> <p>SCP-6009-J were 30 instances of sentient cucumbers (Cucumis sativus) that vocalized upon being consumed by a human subject. These vocalizations were sexually explicit and typically voraphilic in nature.</p> </blockquote> <p>I have to say, as much as I’m not into the general idea here, at least the first line of the description lets us know exactly what we’re in for. I actually didn’t realize this was a -J at first, but at this point I finally noticed.</p> <blockquote> <p>The SCP-6009-J vocalized a moaning sound followed by the phrase, &quot;Radish me, daddy&quot;.</p> </blockquote> <p>One day, you will have to answer for this.</p> <p>I would really love to upvote, but at the moment I don’t feel like the joke goes much further than ‘haha vore’. The interview doesn’t really add to the joke that much, rather just telling it again through the D-Class’ reaction in a way that I don’t feel is as funny as the previous clinical description. I can’t say I didn’t enjoy this, though, so:</p> </div> </div> </div> <p>Novote for the moment, but hoping to turn it into an upvote!</p> <p><sub><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Opinions expressed in this review do not reflect the opinions of SCP Wiki staff as a whole. Please respond to <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" >Tanhony</a></span> or contact the captain of the Site Criticism Team, <span class="printuser"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" >SoullessSingularity</a></span>, for any questions or concerns relating to this review.</sub></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
